| the current versions containg a dash.  That's why it would help if you
| could stick to the same spelling as the authors of lme4 and Matrix have
| choosen to enable us generating versioned dependencies automatically
| inside the pbkrtest package.

Debian is overzealous in the autotests (which I consider less than ideally
designed, but that is a Debian-internal discussion) as well as bossy in this
outreach. It is a missing feature ("bug") in our tooling which should be
fixed on our side.

In any event, my packaging of your pbkrtest package is already taken care of
via this patch which will get auto-applied:

https://salsa.debian.org/edd/r-cran-pbkrtest/blob/master/debian/patches/hyphenated_version

So again, sorry for this mail. I had preemptively tried to not have him send
this, firstly because I disagree on the matter and secondly because he simply
should not meddle on my relationship with my package upstream -- you.  This
is rather disappointing behaviour going against the very team spirit we
usually have. At least on better days.

And I also apologise for him addressing you as 'Michael'. Sigh.

Will I get to see you in Brisbane for useR? We got to continue the "evening
entertainment" tradition from Brussels :)

Cheers, Dirk

